From 06cf7d3311cd11393f587846ddd6af3b619cbd56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:29:31 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/32] kcm_smserver: Form page, session restore first, logind
 questions asynchronous
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Form (docs/page-design.md). Config keys, kcfg, D-Bus calls, defaults unchanged. Not built yet.

Moved / renamed:
- Session restore (login) is the first, untitled section; "Ignored applications" is indented under the restore radios and
  disabled (not hidden) with "Start with an empty session" (kcm_smserver/loginMode, excludeApps).
- "Ask for confirmation: On shutdown, restart, and logout" -> checkbox "Ask for confirmation on shutdown, restart, and
  logout" in section "Logout and Shutdown" (kcm_smserver/confirmLogout; General was a non-noun title, HIG-057).
- Firmware: Switch -> CheckBox "Enter UEFI firmware settings on next restart" (takes effect alone, docs/page-design.md §3);
  section shown only when logind can do it (kcm_smserver/isUefi). Restart Now unchanged (RestartNow).
- Shell name is "Startup & Shutdown" (ia/layout.json), old "Desktop Session" is an alias there.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006 (order by use), HIG-057 (no General/Advanced). Accessible.name on the text field.

Speed cause: the constructor called CanRebootToFirmwareSetup().value() and property("RebootToFirmwareSetup"), both blocking
on the system bus (kcmsmserver.cpp ctor). Now QDBusPendingCallWatcher + async Properties.Get; isUefi and canFirmwareSetup
are NOTIFY properties so the Firmware section appears when logind answers. After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Unconfirmed: org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties.Get result handled as QDBusPendingReply<QDBusVariant> (standard, not compiled).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
